<title>MEXICO: Abaco and Confia are delisted.</title>
<headline>Abaco and Confia are delisted.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares issued by the Mexican financial group Abaco Grupo Financiero SA de CV and its banking unit Banca Confia SNC were delisted from the Mexican Stock Exchange (BMV) on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;As a takeover by a foreign financial institute is under evaluation and with the aim of avoiding disorder in the market ... delisting takes effect today,&quot; an on-line report by the BMV said.</p>
<p>U.S.-based Citicorp and Spanish firm Corporacion Bancaria de Espana had tabled bids to acquire Abaco in early July.</p>
<p>((--Karina Balderas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9562))</p>
